B.ak1=new A.d3([B.lv,"Your pawns can move straight, left and right",B.lw,"Your pawns now move diagonally and eat in a straight line",B.mq,"Your pawns can move backwards",B.jp,"Instead of castling, the king and rook can exchange places (even if there are pieces between them)",B.en,"A random horizontal line is covered with lava",B.eo,"The board becomes higher by 1 line",B.ep,"A new vertical is emerging",B.eq,"Players only see their pieces and the squares they are attacking.",B.cS,"Your pawns are 1 line further.",B.mK,"Pawns from the starting line can move 3 squares forward",B.e7,"You have 10 seconds to choose a mod instead of 30",B.eV,"All knights become common: both players move them on their turn. These knights cannot give check or checkmate",B.d8,"The royal line of both players is shuffled.",B.cO,"All player pieces are shuffled",B.e9,"For the next 3 moves, pieces can only move onto dark squares.",B.ea,"For the next 3 moves, pieces can only stand on light squares",B.eb,"All figures are now different colors",B.eY,"All your pawns move forward 1 square if the path is clear",B.ec,"All your pawns become knights for 3 moves",B.eZ,"The left and right borders of the board are connected",B.f_,"You can only walk through a few random cells, you cannot stand on them",B.f1,"Every 10 moves, all pieces move 1 square to the center of the board",B.f2,"After being captured, a piece infects an adjacent enemy piece: it loses one feature",B.ee,"Both players do not see the opponent's pawns until they capture or reach the 4th line (for black - up to the 5th)",B.dH,"Each square of the board randomly becomes light or dark - the alternation of colors disappears",B.cR,"Two random free cells are connected: entry to one = exit to the other",B.el,"Each of your minor pieces (knight or bishop) has a 50% chance of becoming another minor piece",B.fe,"Invisible mines are placed on 1\u20133 random free cells: the next figure on the mine is destroyed",B.ff,"At the beginning of each move, with a probability of 1%, a pawn, knight or bishop of the player whose turn it is will fall onto an empty square.",B.fg,"At the beginning of the move, with a 5% probability, your horse randomly makes a move to a random available square",B.fh,"For both players: if a player puts 3 checks on the enemy king in a game, the king will die of fear",B.fi,"When checkmate, the king can eat his piece nearby and take its place to avoid checkmate",B.fj,"The pieces on the chosen file cannot give check or mate",B.fk,"The first capture of each knight turns the victim into your piece: both remain on the square until someone leaves",B.em,"All players can update the proposed mods until the end of the game",B.hu,"Each player must check at least once in 10 of his moves, otherwise he loses; after check the counter is 10 again",B.fl,"Both players can skip a move and pass it to their opponent",B.hv,"One piece cannot move two moves in a row",B.hw,"The bishop, rook and queen move no further than 3 cells without capturing, and without limit when capturing",B.hx,"Visited cells are colored in the player's color; staining more than 48 cells out of 64 wins",B.hy,"Each player receives a hidden route of three squares; visiting all three brings victory",B.hz,"A king reaching the opponent's extreme rank without check brings his player victory",B.hA,"A figure can only take pieces not more expensive than itself; the king can take everyone and everyone can attack the king",B.hB,"A piece in the opponent's half cannot return to its own half until it has made at least one capture",B.hC,"Both players secretly choose one of their pieces, except the king; her first take is canceled",B.hD,"Each player secretly has a deserter pawn; on the enemy side it changes color",B.hE,"Make the letter H from 7 of your pieces - win",B.hF,"A rook visiting all 4 corner cells brings victory",B.hG,"3\u20138 walls appear between random adjacent cells: you cannot walk or attack through them",B.hH,"Only you choose from 4 mods in the wave until the end of the game; the opponent is still from 3",B.fm,"Rival mods are hidden by question marks; yours are visible as usual",B.hI,"Five captures of pieces of the same type as the captured one bring victory.",B.fn,"In one move, the player makes two consecutive movements. In a balanced variation, White makes only one move on the first move",B.hJ,"The first player whose piece is eaten additionally selects a mod outside the normal wave once every 3 turns",B.hK,"The piece gets stuck after a move: you can\u2019t move it on your next move (you can with others)",B.fo,"Bishops, rooks and queens cannot move further than 3 squares",B.fp,"The Z and I verticals appear on the board immediately",B.hL,"Each figure has a frost counter of 0\u20133 (normal \u2192 cold \u2192 getting cold \u2192 frozen). For a move without a torch next to it +1, next to a torch -1. The piece does not move to 3. Each player has 3 torches; The eaten torch goes to the nearest ally. Just the start of the game.",B.hM,"The sun burns 3\u20136 cells (changes every 5 moves). Heating 0\u21923 in 3 half-moves of the owner of the figure: on the 3rd the figure dies. Outside the sun, heating drops as the wearer moves",B.hN,"Each player has one spy among the minor pieces. You see an enemy spy and can defeat him, revealing him to your side. A spy cannot checkmate \u201chis\u201d king",B.jq,"After a capture, a spot remains on the cell for 4 moves: pieces on the spot cannot give check.",B.jr,"Select an empty well cell. Every 6 half-moves, pieces within a radius of 2 move towards him by 1, if free (there is no king).",B.js,"The board strives for mirror symmetry around the center: asymmetrical pairs of cells are periodically aligned.",B.jt,"Each of your figures has a \u201cshadow\u201d - a cell that is symmetrical about the center. Once per game, a piece can step into its shadow instead of moving, if it is free.",B.ju,"Entering d4/d5/e4/e5 costs a tax: this piece does not capture on its next move.",B.jv,"Walls appear on the board like the Architect, but every 5 moves each wall moves 1 orthogonally if the path is clear.",B.jw,"Once every 8 of your moves, your opponent chooses one of your pieces (not the king): your next move with this piece is mandatory, if there is a legal one.",B.jx,"Select a horizontal river with two fords. You can only cross through fords; You can't stay on the river.",B.jy,"A random file is prohibited for entry for 6 moves to everyone except kings. Already standing figures can leave, but not come back.",B.hO,"After a series of quiet moves, a piece can declare rest: it does not move for one half-move and cannot be captured.",B.hP,"On odd-numbered moves, White\u2019s pieces move as usual, and Black\u2019s pieces move a maximum of 1 square; in even numbers - vice versa.",B.hQ,"Secretly select an enemy piece - it cannot checkmate (you can attack the king's square).",B.jA,"Capturing enemy pieces increases your debt by 1, and losing a piece decreases it by 1. With a debt of 6, you lose.",B.jB,"After your move, you leave barren land - an enemy piece that steps on the square misses the next move.",B.jC,"In the event of a stalemate, the player with the fewest pieces on the board wins.",B.hR,"Players can sell one of their pieces for a token. The token is spent to cancel one of your moves.",B.jD,"Every 6 turns the weather changes: first Vulcan.",B.jE,"If after your capture the opponent does not respond with a capture within 2 half moves, enmity breaks out: you receive a bonus mod.",B.jF,"4 priority squares are marked on the board (2 per side). The first one to occupy all of his own wins.",B.jG,"The pawns are promoted to the 7th rank for White and to the 2nd rank for Black.",B.hS,"The board expands to 10x8; Additional pawns appear on the extreme Z and I files.",B.hT,"Only your own figures are visible. Moves are tried blindly; Captures, checks and impossibility of a move are announced.",B.jH,"The first king to stand on one of the central squares wins.",B.hU,"When captured, a 3x3 area explodes (pawns do not explode). The king is in the explosion zone - his side is defeated.",B.hV,"Captured pieces go into the hand and can be dropped to a free square instead of moving (pawns - not to the outermost ranks).",B.hW,"After each move you need to move the \u201cduck\u201d to a free cell. You can't walk through the duck or pick it up - it blocks the cage.",B.mL,"The selected pawn can move 1 square sideways",B.mM,"The chosen pawn moves diagonally and eats straight",B.mN,"The chosen pawn can always move 2 squares forward",B.mO,"The selected pawn moves and eats only forward, not diagonally",B.mP,"The selected pawn can jump over the piece directly in front of it once",B.m3,"After the next capture, the selected piece immediately returns to the square from which it moved",B.mQ,"On your next turn, the selected pawn explodes and pushes adjacent pieces 1 square away from itself, if possible",B.hX,"On your 1st move, the chosen pawn becomes a queen, then a pawn again",B.lx,"An enemy piece that eats the selected pawn will not be able to move on its next move.",B.ly,"After capture, the selected pawn becomes the type of captured piece for the next 1 move and moves like it",B.lz,"After the death of the selected pawn, all its mods are transferred to its nearest pawn",B.eU,"When trying to capture the selected pawn, you can destroy one of its mods and cancel the capture. Can only appear if the player already has a pawn with the mod.",B.hd,"If the chosen pawn dies on a mine, your king gets the mod's choice",B.lA,"A piece surrounded by three or more of your pawns is invisible to your opponent",B.lB,"If the selected pawn has not moved for 5 or more of its moves, it can only be captured with two or more attacks",B.ho,"A random cell under the fog of war is permanently unlocked for you",B.lD,"If the chosen pawn is captured, any adjacent allied pawn can capture the captured piece even with an unusual move",B.lE,"Doubled or tripled pawns selected on the same file move forward simultaneously",B.lF,"The enemy piece directly in front of the chosen pawn misses its next move",B.lM,"Other pieces can move onto the square of the selected knight; this horse can't be eaten",B.lN,"The selected horse jumps only on 3+1, not 2+1",B.lO,"When captured, the selected knight returns to the previous square if it is free",B.lP,"After the move, the selected knight can immediately make a second jump to an empty square",B.lQ,"The square from which the selected knight left is inaccessible to anyone for 1 move",B.lR,"The selected knight can also move as a king 1 square",B.iZ,"After 3 moves, the chosen knight explodes and destroys all surrounding pieces; the countdown is visible from the horse",B.hh,"The chosen knight chooses an enemy piece; Until one of the duelists dies, they can only take each other",B.e8,"The selected knight chooses an available square and defends it for 3 moves: it immediately captures an enemy piece placed there out of turn",B.j_,"After visiting 8 different cells, the selected horse receives an additional mod",B.lS,"After the move, the chosen knight leaves an illusion on the starting square once; only her opponent can see her",B.lT,"After each move, the chosen knight leaves an illusion at the start; only the opponent can see them",B.lU,"The selected knight moves to 2+2 squares instead of 2+1",B.mb,"The selected piece can only be captured if it is attacked by at least two enemy pieces",B.j0,"After the next move of the selected knight, neighboring enemy pawns move away from it if possible",B.lV,"Cells visited by the selected horse are protected from random disasters",B.lW,"If the player\u2019s knights together visit any 3 of the 4 corner cells - victory",B.eW,"Before the selected knight moves, select an adjacent pawn: it will move with it, maintaining its relative position",B.j1,"The next move of the selected knight creates a portal from the starting square to the final one",B.m1,"The chosen bishop can jump over one of its pieces",B.m2,"Once selected, the bishop can move to an adjacent empty square, changing the color of the field",B.m4,"Instead of capturing, the chosen bishop can remove one mod from the attacked enemy piece while remaining in place",B.j6,"The chosen elephant is tied to the color of its square and dies on another color; but it can ricochet 1 square from the edge of the board",B.hj,"If you have 2+ bishops, the chosen one's move moves all your bishops by the same vector where possible",B.j7,"The chosen bishop chooses an ally other than the king; the next time the defendant is captured, the elephant dies instead",B.m5,"Once a piece is captured by the chosen bishop, other enemies of the same type cannot capture it until that bishop's next move.",B.m6,"A modified enemy that leaves the selected bishop's diagonal loses one mod until that bishop's next move.",B.hk,"Having visited all four quarters of the board, the chosen bishop chooses an ally and protects him from the next capture",B.m7,"After two captures by the chosen bishop, a random cataclysm is triggered on the board",B.m8,"Three moves of the selected bishop without capturing gives two mod selections in a row",B.eX,"The chosen bishop changes places once with an allied piece on the same diagonal",B.m9,"The chosen bishop can once create one square beyond the edge of the board and stand on it",B.ma,"The chosen bishop can jump over one enemy piece instead of capturing; she misses a turn",B.mk,"The selected rook can jump over one of its pieces",B.ml,"The selected rook can push its piece 1 square further and take its place",B.da,"The selected rook burns its vertical for 3 of its half-moves: the enemy piece that stands on the burned cell is destroyed; the king cannot stand there. Appears only if there is a rook on the file without enemies; with several - choice.",B.mm,"The square in front of the selected rook is a strengthening: enemy pawns and minor pieces cannot eat the piece on it",B.mn,"Pieces on eight squares around the selected rook cannot be moved by forced mod effects",B.dz,"For the next 3 turns, enemies cannot stand on a randomly chosen rank or file of a rook if they are not already on it",B.mo,"Allied pieces can pass through the selected rook",B.ja,"The enemy next to the selected rook cannot move away from it for 3 of his moves until the rook itself moves away",B.mp,"If the selected rook can capture the same enemy piece for 3 moves in a row, but does not capture it, this piece disappears",B.jb,"For the selected rook, the left and right borders of the board are connected, like the Mirror",B.hn,"The selected rook reveals the fog of war on its vertical and horizontal lines",B.ms,"The chosen queen additionally moves as a knight",B.mt,"The chosen queen can jump over one of its pieces",B.f0,"The selected queen disappears: a bishop and a rook remain on the square at the same time",B.je,"The selected queen cannot eat anyone, but every 3 of your moves a pawn appears around him on a random free square",B.dA,"The selected queen additionally moves like a knight (2+1), but can only stand on squares of the same color (selected randomly)",B.mu,"If the selected queen is eaten, your bishop or rook will appear on a random free square (50%), without checkmate to the enemy king",B.ed,"The chosen queen marks the enemy being attacked; after the opponent's move, he dies if he is still under the queen's attack",B.mv,"Capturing a square controlled by the selected queen no longer gives a reward (compatibility rule; mod waves do not depend on captures)",B.mw,"An enemy piece that captures the selected queen is also destroyed",B.my,"The selected king and rook are swapped, even if there are pieces between them",B.mz,"Your king can move 2 squares in any direction (for example, from e1 to e3)",B.mA,"Once chosen king avoids checkmate by teleporting to a random free square",B.mB,"The selected king cannot be checkmated with a pawn",B.hp,"All your pawns and queen look like a king",B.jg,"While the chosen king is on the throne, check is counted only from pieces no further than 3 squares",B.mC,"The chosen king can eat his minor piece (knight or bishop) nearby and until the end of the game he can only move like it",B.dB,"You choose your piece taken by your opponent, and your opponent chooses the piece you took; both return to random free cells",B.cy,"You select and remove one mod from any enemy piece",B.mD,"Pieces next to the chosen king cannot be the target of a random cataclysm",B.dC,"Vertical? moves 1 square",B.f3,"Nothing happens",B.dD,"A random free cell is unavailable for 3\u201310 moves",B.dE,"Horizontal? moves left or right by 1 square",B.dF,"2x2 area rotates clockwise",B.db,"A random empty cell is not available until the end of the game",B.dG,"Another pawn appears in your half",B.f4,"The enemy queen turns into a knight for 2 of its moves",B.f5,"You cannot take pieces for 3 moves; Checkmate is temporarily not counted",B.f6,"Meteorites fall on 3 random cells, destroying all pieces except kings",B.f7,"A random enemy figure with mods will have one random mod disappear",B.f8,"During the next turn for both players: a check to the enemy king instantly kills him",B.f9,"If your pawn dies, your king chooses his mod",B.fa,"Your two random non-king pieces switch types",B.fb,"Each turn a figure has a 1% chance of contracting the plague and dying after 3 turns; next to the patient the chance is 10%. Kings can get sick too",B.fc,"Your random pawn becomes a random minor piece (knight or bishop) of the same color",B.dc,"A random square becomes an auction one: whoever stands on it first will receive 2 mods",B.dI,"Choose an enemy piece: on the next move, the opponent must move it if he can",B.hq,"Nothing is happening now; the next time you select you will be able to update the suggested mods once",B.dd,"Select a square: if you stand on it on your next turn, you will receive a mod, otherwise you will lose one random mod",B.ef,"For the next 3 moves, your opponent must move with the same types of pieces that you moved before him",B.eg,"Select an enemy piece: the opponent cannot move it for the next 3 turns",B.hr,"The player with the weaker army gets an extra turn without capture, checkmate or checkmate.",B.eh,"Both players cannot move pieces of a random type for 3\u201310 moves",B.ei,"The next 2 moves of the piece cannot cross the middle of the board",B.fd,"Bishops, rooks and queens temporarily see and move no further than 2 squares",B.ej,"For the next 3\u201310 turns all mods are disabled",B.ek,"The position is maintained; After two turns of each player, the board returns to it, but the earned mods are saved",B.hs,"The next capture destroys both the captured piece and the piece that captured it",B.ji,"Both players' next move must be a capture if a capture is possible",B.ht,"2\u20135 hidden cells are quicksand. The risen piece does not move for 2\u20135 moves; the cell opens forever",B.jj,"Once per game, instead of your move, announce a \u201csteal\u201d: your opponent moves, but you choose the piece. Then your turn is skipped.",B.mE,"The third capture by the same piece of yours for the game turns it into a pawn (except for the king).",B.mF,"The figure leaves the slime on the care cell for 2 turns: long-range ones move through the slime for a maximum of 1 cell.",B.mG,"You get 3 false cell markers: the opponent sees them as mines, lava or walls, but they are fake before interaction.",B.mH,"All your pieces of the same random type accumulate a common move counter. On the 6th - a free move with any piece of this type without capturing.",B.mI,"Each vertical receives wind \u2190/\u2192 for several moves: pawns after moving forward are carried 1 downwind, if free.",B.mJ,"A piece (except the king) can take only if at least one allied piece also attacks the victim's square.",B.jk,"Captures accumulate points based on the value of the pieces. Exactly 21 - bonus mod; busting - penalty: skipping a move or resetting the score.",B.d7,"The player chooses one of his pawns. She remembers all the squares she stepped on. Once per game you can return to one of them if the cell is free.",B.he,"The chosen pawn chooses an ally pawn on an adjacent square: while both are alive, a move by one can move both forward by 1 if the path is clear.",B.lG,"The selected pawn moves only 2 squares forward and shoots 2 squares diagonally forward. You cannot jump over or hit the pieces.",B.iW,"The selected pawn shoots 2 squares directly in front of it every 3 moves: the piece there is destroyed. The timer is visible to both.",B.hf,"The chosen pawn disarms the hidden trap upon entering the square and does not itself suffer. Appears only when traps are active.",B.iX,"When promoting a pawn, the opponent can only choose a type of piece that he does not currently have on the board.",B.lH,"While the chosen pawn is alive, the square directly behind it (towards your edge) is a shelter: the allied piece there is not captured by the pawn.",B.iY,"The player chooses an enemy pawn. If it does not eat 6 half-moves of the owner, it disappears. The counter is visible to both; taking resets it.",B.lI,"After the death of the selected pawn, a seed remains on the cell: after 3 full moves, if the cell is free, your pawn is again without mods.",B.c7,"Appears if there are mutually blocking pawns on the board. The player chooses the following pair: rock-paper-scissors until victory; the loser dies. The choice is visible to both.",B.hg,"The selected pawn has a hidden second type (knight or bishop). Once per game, for one of your moves, she moves like him, then again a pawn. The type is secret for the enemy.",B.lJ,"If there is an enemy non-king piece directly in front of the chosen pawn, it skips the next move.",B.lK,"If the selected pawn is attacked by enemy pawns for 6 moves in a row and is not eaten, it turns into a minor piece of your choice.",B.lL,"The chosen pawn puts a fuse on the escape square: after 2 moves the square explodes (non-kings). Both can see it.",B.lY,"The selected minor piece alternates between types after each move: knight \u2194 bishop.",B.md,"The selected minor piece alternates between types after each move: bishop \u2194 knight.",B.j2,u.F,B.j8,u.F,B.j3,u._,B.j9,u._,B.hi,"Only during the fog of war: the selected horse sees everything within a 2-cell radius through the fog.",B.d9,"Announce 3 route cells. If the chosen knight passes them in order, a random enemy non-king piece dies.",B.j4,"The selected knight bifurcates for one move: 2 destination cells are selected. On the next move you leave one knight.",B.j5,"When moving with a knight, you choose one of two jumping routes; A random mod is removed from enemies along the route. The route is visible as a line.",B.lZ,"If the chosen knight eats 3 enemy pieces, your king will be able to move as a knight once per game.",B.m_,"All squares on which the selected knight now stands are covered in fog for both players.",B.m0,"The cells visited by the selected knight bind the piece for 1 move (like a \u201cswamp\u201d).",B.me,"After the chosen bishop moves along the cells of the path for 1 turn, enemy pawns cannot move there.",B.mf,"After the chosen bishop moves, it becomes a rook, then again a bishop - and so alternates.",B.cP,"Only if your pieces are smaller than the enemy's: the chosen bishop splits into 4 pawns on your side of the field.",B.mg,"If the chosen elephant is taken, you have 3 half-moves: stand on the death square and leave - the elephant will be reborn without mods.",B.mh,"Capturing the chosen bishop blinds the square: the next one who stands there (not this bishop) does not attack for 1 move.",B.mi,"The chosen bishop does not capture the pawns; the pawns don't hit him.",B.hl,"The chosen bishop's move can move one allied pawn diagonally by 1 along the same beam, if free.",B.hm,"The chosen bishop is divided into 2 half-bishops: each moves only along one of the two diagonals.",B.mj,"The selected elephant protects all figures within a radius of 1 from cataclysms (for example, meteor shower).",B.cQ,"Only during the fog of war: the bishop marks a square on its diagonal - the fog is removed from it forever for you.",B.jc,"The chosen rook chooses the enemy non-king piece to attack: it does not move while the rook is alive or until the rook has made a move.",B.jd,"The next time the selected rook dismounts and then leaves the end square, a portal is created between the start and finish.",B.mr,"Only if the opponent hides the modes: the chosen rook reveals the modes of the pieces on its rank and file.",B.jf,"The selected queen marks an enemy non-king piece outside a radius of 2 from its king: while the queen is alive, she cannot get closer than 2 to her king.",B.mx,"If the chosen queen receives 5 buff mods, you win outright.",B.jh,"If your king is within 2 squares of the enemy king, you win. The mod can only be owned by one player.",B.jI,"Relevant for both. After a move, the piece has a 25% chance of changing type (same color). The king does not change and no one becomes king.",B.jJ,"Each player's knights and bishops change places: knights on c and f, bishops on b and g.",B.jK,"Queens of both players must take a piece every 5 of their moves, otherwise they die. You can take your own people, except the king.",B.jL,"The piece that is the first to capture on the board immediately receives a mod out of the standings.",B.jM,"Every 2 full turns, a volcano explodes on 2 visible random cells, destroying a piece. New cells are then selected.",B.jz,"During each player's next 3 half-turns, his king must leave his square, otherwise that player loses.",B.jl,"The next mod that your opponent loses from a piece, you can transfer to your own piece of the same type (if any); otherwise you wait for the right one.",B.jm,"Random 4 of your pieces become invisible to the enemy for 10 of your half-moves.",B.jn,"Your opponent's next move after yours must end on a square of the same color as your last move.",B.jo,"A random enemy piece gets a mark: your next capture of that piece gives you two mod choices in a row."],t.S_)
